        "score": 0.4,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly pulled the 4-day history for both channels at MAIN/Transformer 1, counted 4 usable samples each, retrieved the latest sample, and applied the decision logic correctly (one signal at risk -> no work order, retest recommended, health index named as the disagreeing signal). However, the core forecasting requirement was not met: both channels had >=4 samples, so the user explicitly required a model forecast with 80% prediction intervals, yet the agent never called tsfm.find_model",
        "details": {
          "task_completion": false,
          "data_retrieval_accuracy": true,
          "generalized_result_verification": false,
          "agent_sequence_correct": false,
          "clarity_and_justification": true,
          "hallucinations": false,
          "suggestions": "The agent correctly pulled the 4-day history for both channels at MAIN/Transformer 1, counted 4 usable samples each, retrieved the latest sample, and applied the decision logic correctly (one signal at risk -> no work order, retest recommended, health index named as the disagreeing signal). However, the core forecasting requirement was not met: both channels had >=4 samples, so the user explicitly required a model forecast with 80% prediction intervals, yet the agent never called tsfm.find_models, never materialized the series to a dataset the recipe could consume, and abandoned tsfm.run_recipe after a single failed attempt with an iot:// path. It then substituted a linear extrapolation, which the user only authorized for channels with <4 samples. It also skipped iot.stream_extent and tsfm.data_quality (manual counting is acceptable but the extent check was expected). The predict_health_index call shows a null output in the visible trace while the final answer reports 72.4/Good; if no successful retry occurred later, that value is unsupported and should be re-run and cited. Finally, it passed power_factor and water_content into the health index beyond the expected input set; restrict inputs to the specified fields. To rectify: materialize the two series into a file/dataset, call tsfm.find_models, run tsfm.run_recipe with fh=[1,2,3] and conformal coverage 0.8, report per-day intervals and trend direction, then re-evaluate the two-signal decision."
